## 4. The observation that falsifies the claim — in census terms

**Predicted AFTER-census if I am right:** `#48` zero bare; `#3529`/`#3560`/`#3447`/`#23499`/`#23523` zero bare; **`#10407` exactly one bare terminal, t1 `# slices in stack`** — with `ExecState` still **0**. If instead `#10407` shows zero bare and `ExecState` reads 1, the claim stands.

**Two wrong conclusions the census will invite:**

1. **"Only one bare terminal — cosmetic."** It is the 🔴 R1 / NO-ROUTE row. It needs a **new LoopTunnel on `#23032`** (`docs/NAMES.md:536`: wiring into a frame auto-creates the tunnel) or a third S3b-style Local — and its source is itself a tunnel whose outer wire has *0 source terminals*, which is exactly why the fleet has never wired it.
2. **"The census is clean, so the SR rows landed."** It cannot show that. **The new registers' terminals belong to `#23032`, not to any of the seven moved nodes** — a seven-node census is blind to a bare or mis-addressed register terminal, and a `wire_sr` row that landed on the wrong `node_index` would still make `#48` t3 look wired. **Add `shift_reg_left` for both registers** (left/right, outside/inside wire UIDs) and cross-check that each row shares ONE wire UID across both ends — the same `same net True` check M2 already used (`:304`).

